{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Leo, sorry the VPN is giving you trouble in Lisbon. Your account, VPN access and Duo setup all look fine, and your VPN connected from Lisbon this morning and on the past few days. That points to the hotel connection or the VPN app, not your account. Please try these steps in order:\n1. With the VPN off, open any public website in your browser. If the hotel Wi-Fi shows a sign-in or 'accept terms' page, complete it (you may have to do this again each day or after reconnecting). Then connect the VPN.\n2. If it still fails, quit the VPN app completely, reopen it and try again. If that doesn't work, restart your laptop.\n3. If you're asked for a Duo push that never shows up, open Duo Mobile on your phone, pull down to refresh, and make sure notifications are turned on for Duo.\nIf none of this works, please reply and tell us: (a) whether public websites load without the VPN, and (b) the exact error message the VPN app shows. We'll take it from there. If you're short on time, using your phone's hotspot for the VPN is a quick workaround.\nAlso, your laptop is almost out of disk space (about 9 GB free). That won't stop the VPN, but when you have a moment, clearing out old downloads will help keep things running smoothly.",
  "internal_note": "Checked per KB-013/KB-016. Account active, failed_login_count 0, sign_in_blocked false, vpn_access true. Duo enrolled (duo_push, Leo's phone). Sign-in logs: daily successful VPN sign-ins from Lisbon, PT (198.51.100.66) on 10/07, 10/08 and 10/09 08:05 UTC, all with Duo. These match the reported trip (09:05 local) and show no failed_password or mfa_denied entries. The current failed attempts are not in the logs, so they are likely not reaching the server. Most likely cause is the hotel captive portal or a client-side issue. Laptop BL-LT-0106 is online (last check-in 14:35 UTC) with a low disk space warning (3.5% free, 9 GB). Sent the user the KB-013 fix steps (captive portal, restart VPN client/laptop, Duo refresh) and asked whether public internet works without VPN and for the exact error. If he says internet works and the steps fail, escalate to Tier 2 per KB-013. If he has no internet, follow KB-014. Nothing queued.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-013",
    "KB-016"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
